Make the voxel mod survive the removal of src/render/GBCFX.lua.

Gen1Recomp deleted that module between 0.2.20 and 0.2.24, replacing it with
src/render/ShaderFX.lua. DRAMALESS_SHAPE still requires it in two places as of 2.0.3, the latest
release, and neither survives it:

  main.lua:267  require("src.render.GBCFX").setLevel(0)
  main.lua:308  pcall(require("src.render.GBCFX").setLevel, 0)

The second only looks guarded. The pcall wraps the CALL; the require is an
argument, so it is evaluated first and throws on its own.

Line 308 sits at the top of pinEngineFx, which is the first statement of the
mod's "ui.options.rows" hook. src/mods/Hooks.lua runs every link under pcall and
logs-and-skips one that throws, so the wrapper dies before insertGrouped and the
mod's rows never reach OPTIONS. On a handheld that is the whole control surface:
the mod's own hotkeys are keyboard-only (v/g/t/c via Game.keypressed, no gamepad
binding), so a player loses every way to turn 3D on or off, with nothing on
screen to explain it.

Upstream will not shim it -- bryanthaboi/gen1recomp#1823 was closed by the engine
author as "this is a mod issue". Reported to the mod author as
artyrambles/DRAMALESS_SHAPE#53; drop this patch when a release carries the fix.

The replacement is the shape Gen1Recomp itself used at src/import/LauncherSettings.lua
while the module still existed: pcall the require, then use the result.

verify.sh asserts both ends of this -- that no bare require of the module is left
in the staged mod, and that game/src/render/GBCFX.lua has NOT come back upstream
(if it does, this patch is obsolete and must be deleted rather than carried).

--- a/main.lua
--- a/main.lua
+++ b/main.lua
@@ -264,7 +264,8 @@
           Pipelines.syncOptions(self.save.options)
           self.save.options.tilt, self.save.options.gbcfx = 0, 0
           require("src.render.Tilt").setLevel(0)
-          require("src.render.GBCFX").setLevel(0)
+          local okFx, GBCFX = pcall(require, "src.render.GBCFX")
+          if okFx then GBCFX.setLevel(0) end
           self:writeOptions()
           V.log:event("options", "hotkey", { key = key })
           return
@@ -305,7 +306,8 @@
   local changed = opts and ((opts.tilt or 0) ~= 0 or (opts.gbcfx or 0) ~= 0)
   if opts then opts.tilt, opts.gbcfx = 0, 0 end
   pcall(require("src.render.Tilt").setLevel, 0)
-  pcall(require("src.render.GBCFX").setLevel, 0)
+  local okFx, GBCFX = pcall(require, "src.render.GBCFX")
+  if okFx then pcall(GBCFX.setLevel, 0) end
   if changed and game.writeOptions then pcall(game.writeOptions, game) end
 end
 
